# Dependencies
/node_modules

# Production
/build

# Generated files
.docusaurus
.cache-loader
# Deliberately gitignored, not a gap: this is build-only, submodule-synced
# content with no independent source of truth to drift from — unlike
# docs/intro.mdx and every product's own index.mdx/ROS/index.mdx, which
# *are* committed and checked for drift in ci.yml's "Verify generated
# content is committed" step.
#
# Every page scripts/sync-external-docs.js produces under software-tools/
# — a synced README partial, a synced docs/ guide, or the whole
# doxygen2docusaurus API tree — is plain CommonMark (.md); every
# hand-authored wrapper/landing page (including a folder's own index.mdx
# sitting next to synced siblings, e.g.
# software-tools/<Product>/<Tool>/docs/index.mdx) is MDX (.mdx) — see the
# `markdown.format: 'detect'` comment in docusaurus.config.js, which relies on
# that same split. One generic pattern by extension, not a per-product path
# list: covers every current product (Adaptive grippers, EPick, Force
# Torque Sensor, Tactile Sensor) and any future one with no edit needed
# here when a new tool repo is onboarded — see "Checklist: onboarding a
# new C++ tool repo" in docs/contribute/api-reference-cpp.mdx.
software-tools/**/*.md
# Exception: Force Torque Sensor's C driver has no submodule/sync job in
# external-jobs.js yet (unlike every other _readme.md under
# software-tools/) — this one is a plain static file its wrapper
# index.mdx imports directly, so it must stay tracked despite the
# extension. Confirmed the only one: `find software-tools -iname '*.md'
# -not -iname '*.mdx'` cross-checked against every job's actual output
# before adding the blanket rule above.
!software-tools/Force Torque Sensor/Libraries/C/_readme.md

# Stable's own Docusaurus version — used to be committed as a permanent,
# deliberate snapshot; isn't anymore. Every build now re-derives it fresh
# from source (scripts/ensure-stable-version.js, run via the `generate`
# prebuild hook — see docs/contribute/versioning.mdx), the exact same way
# software-tools/**/*.md above is: not because nothing decides its
# content, but because that decision — which tag each tool's Stable
# should track — lives in the one small file that *does* stay committed,
# software-tools-stable.json. Regenerating this from that file on every
# build, rather than freezing and committing the result once, is what
# stops Stable's content from being a full second copy of Latest's own
# content sitting in the repo.
software-tools_versioned_docs/
software-tools_versioned_sidebars/
software-tools_versions.json
# scripts/ensure-stable-version.js's own local cache — lets a repeated
# `npm start` during a normal dev session skip re-materializing Stable
# when software-tools-stable.json hasn't changed since the last run in
# this same working directory. Purely local bookkeeping, not something
# any other checkout needs to see.
/.stable-materialized.json

# doxygen2docusaurus scratch output (scripts/sync-external-docs.js stages
# here, then copies the filtered result into docs/ — see external-jobs.js)
/.doxygen2docusaurus-staging
/doxygen2docusaurus.json
/scripts/generated/

# scripts/auto-cut-versions.js's own scratch output — read by
# .github/workflows/cut-versions.yml, never committed itself.
/cut-version-summary.md

# Editor / machine-specific
.vscode/

# Misc
.DS_Store
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local

npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
